  "title": "Your puppy's first 30 days: a calm, confident start",
  "shortTitle": "Puppy's first 30 days",
  "excerpt": "Crate comfort, toilet routines, first walks and the socialisation checklist our trainers swear by.",
  "date": "28 Aug 2026",
  "datetime": "2026-08-28",
  "readTime": "8 min read",
  "author": {
   "name": "Dr. Meera Kulkarni",
   "role": "Consulting vet · Reviewed by Neha Joshi",
   "bio": "BVSc & AH, consulting vet for Wag & Whisker. Meera runs our monthly free puppy clinics and shares her home with two Indies and a very bossy cat.",
   "initials": "MK",
   "tint": "tint-cats"
  },
  "metaDesc": "A vet-reviewed plan for your puppy's first month: crate setup, toilet training, socialisation, vaccinations and a printable 30-day checklist.",
  "heroImg": "blog-puppy",
  "heroAlt": "A golden retriever puppy walking on a lead across a leafy lawn",
  "lead": "Bringing home a puppy is pure joy, and a little chaos. The first month shapes how your dog sees the world, so a calm, consistent start pays off for years. Here's the plan our trainers and vets share with every new puppy family.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "id": "before",
    "title": "Before your puppy comes home",
    "html": "<p>Choose a quiet corner for a crate or pen, and puppy-proof anything at nose height: cables, shoes, houseplants and bins. Stock up on the food your breeder or shelter used so tummies don't get upset by a sudden change.</p><ul><li>A crate or pen big enough to stand, turn and stretch in</li><li>Two bowls, a lightweight collar with ID tag and a 1.5 m leash</li><li>Three or four toys of different textures, including one to chew</li><li>Enzyme cleaner for accidents (they will happen!)</li></ul>"
   },
   {
    "id": "week-one",
    "title": "Week one: settling in",
    "html": "<p>Keep the first few days boring on purpose. Limit visitors, follow the same routine for meals, naps and play, and let your puppy explore one room at a time. Puppies sleep 18–20 hours a day. Protect those naps.</p><blockquote>“Predictability is the best comfort you can give a puppy. When they know what comes next, they relax, and relaxed puppies learn faster.” — Neha Joshi, head groomer &amp; trainer</blockquote>"
   },
   {
    "id": "toilet",
    "title": "Toilet training that actually works",
    "html": "<p>Take your puppy outside after every nap, meal and play session, and every two hours in between. Use the same spot and a cue word, and celebrate the moment they finish with a tiny treat. Never punish accidents. Just clean up with an enzyme spray and supervise more closely.</p><div class=\"tip-box\"><svg class=\"icon\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"M12 16v-4\"/><path d=\"M12 8h.01\"/></svg><p><strong>Trainer tip:</strong> A puppy can usually hold its bladder for about one hour per month of age, plus one. A three-month-old needs a break roughly every four hours overnight.</p></div>"
   },
   {
    "id": "social",
    "title": "The socialisation window",
    "html": "<p>Between three and fourteen weeks, puppies are wired to accept new things. Aim for gentle, positive exposure to different people, surfaces, sounds and calm, vaccinated dogs. Quality beats quantity: one good experience is worth ten overwhelming ones.</p>"
   },
   {
    "id": "vet",
    "title": "Vet visits & vaccinations",
    "html": "<p>Book a check-up in the first week. Your vet will plan core vaccinations, deworming and flea prevention, and can microchip at the same visit. Ask about our Puppy Intro groom too. A short, treat-filled first visit makes future grooms much easier.</p>"
   },
   {
    "id": "checklist",
    "title": "Your 30-day checklist",
    "html": "<ol><li>Crate set up and puppy-proofing done</li><li>First vet visit booked and vaccination plan agreed</li><li>Toilet routine and cue word in place</li><li>Ten new, positive experiences each week</li><li>Name, sit and “touch” started in 2-minute sessions</li><li>Puppy Intro groom booked around week four</li></ol>"
   }
  ],
